.TH PYTHIA "1" "October 2026" "pythia 0.5.23" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pythia \- game library manager for your computers and handhelds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pythia
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,URI\/\fR]
.br
.B pythia
\fB\-\-ui\fR \fI\,desktop|bigpicture|web\/\fR [\fB\-\-error\-console\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pythia tracks which versions of which games exist on which of your computers and
handhelds. While it runs, it is this computer's droidtop agent: paired droidtop
handhelds sync their library and saves with it.
.PP
With no option, or with \fB\-\-ui\fR, Pythia opens its window. Any other option runs
the command line interface and needs no display.
.PP
\fIURI\fR is a pythia:rungame/<slug>, pythia:rungameid/<id> or pythia:install/<slug> URI.
.SS "Interface:"
.TP
\fB\-\-ui\fR \fI\,desktop|bigpicture|web\/\fR
Open this front end.
.TP
\fB\-\-error\-console\fR
Show the error console in the web front end.
.SS "Options:"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version of Pythia and exit.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR
Show debug messages.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-install\fR \fI\,FILE_OR_URL\/\fR
Install a game from a yml file.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Force updates.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-output\-script\fR \fI\,GAME\/\fR
Generate a bash script to run a game without the client.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-exec\fR \fI\,COMMAND\/\fR
Execute a program with the Pythia Runtime.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\-games\fR
List all games in the database.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-installed\fR
Only list installed games.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-list\-steam\-games\fR
List available Steam games.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-steam\-folders\fR
List all known Steam library folders.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-runners\fR
List all known runners.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-wine\-versions\fR
List all known Wine versions.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-list\-all\-service\-games\fR
List all games for all services in the database.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-service\-games\fR \fI\,SERVICE\/\fR
List all games for the given service in the database.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-install\-runner\fR \fI\,RUNNER\/\fR
Install a runner.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-uninstall\-runner\fR \fI\,RUNNER\/\fR
Uninstall a runner.
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR \fI\,SLUG\/\fR
Export a game.
.TP
\fB\-\-import\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Import a game.
.TP
\fB\-\-dest\fR \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Destination path for export or import.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Display the list of games in JSON format.
.TP
\fB\-\-reinstall\fR
Reinstall a game.
.SS "droidtop (this computer as the droidtop agent of paired handhelds):"
.TP
\fB\-\-droidtop\-serve\fR
Serve paired droidtop handhelds until stopped.
.TP
\fB\-\-droidtop\-pair\fR \fI\,CODE\/\fR
Pair with a handheld showing CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-droidtop\-pair\-show\fR
Show a code and this computer's addresses for a handheld to pair.
.TP
\fB\-\-droidtop\-devices\fR
List the paired handhelds.
.TP
\fB\-\-droidtop\-unpair\fR \fI\,ID\/\fR
Forget a paired handheld (the start of its id is enough).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
https://github.com/bi0shacker001/pythia
.PP
Pythia is largely based on Lutris (https://lutris.net).
